{%- liquid
  comment
    Scroll-expand hero — port of the ScrollExpandMedia React component.

    Behaviour reproduced:
      · full-bleed background fading out as the media opens
      · a centred media frame that opens from a small window to full width
      · the title splitting on the first space, the halves parting like curtains
      · below-media content arriving at progress >= 0.75

    Three deliberate departures from the React source, all of them fixes:

    1. GSAP ScrollTrigger pin + scrub instead of hijacking `wheel` and calling
       preventDefault. The wheel-hijack breaks trackpad momentum, breaks iOS
       Safari, and fights Shopify's own scroll listeners.

    2. The frame is laid out at its FINAL size and opens via `clip-path: inset`,
       with the media counter-scaled inside. The React source animates width and
       height in pixels, which forces layout on every frame — that is why it
       stuttered. Nothing here touches layout.

    3. Translate directions are computed from document.dir, so the curtains part
       correctly in RTL instead of being hardcoded LTR.

    Fallbacks: no JS, no GSAP, or prefers-reduced-motion → `hero--static`, which
    is the fully-open resting state. It looks intentional, not broken.
  endcomment

  assign heading = section.settings.heading
  assign words = heading | split: ' '
  assign first_word = words | first
  assign rest_words = ''
  if words.size > 1
    assign rest_words = heading | remove_first: first_word | strip
  endif

  assign video = section.settings.video
  assign poster = section.settings.poster
  if poster == blank and video != blank
    assign poster = video.preview_image
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  No `hero--static` in the server render. The base CSS state is the fully-open
  hero, so JS-off visitors get a finished-looking hero; the script below adds
  `hero--static` (or the collapsed start state) synchronously before first
  paint, so neither path costs a layout shift.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section
  class="hero"
  id="hero-{{ section.id }}"
  data-hero
>
  <div class="hero__stage" data-hero-stage>
    {%- comment -%}
      Background. This is the LCP element on the homepage, so it is eager with
      fetchpriority="high" and never lazy.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="hero__bg" data-hero-bg>
      {%- if section.settings.background != blank -%}
        <img
          src="{{ section.settings.background | image_url: width: 2400 }}"
          srcset="
            {{ section.settings.background | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w,
            {{ section.settings.background | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w,
            {{ section.settings.background | image_url: width: 1800 }} 1800w,
            {{ section.settings.background | image_url: width: 2400 }} 2400w
          "
          sizes="100vw"
          alt=""
          width="{{ section.settings.background.width }}"
          height="{{ section.settings.background.height }}"
          fetchpriority="high"
          decoding="async"
        >
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <h1 class="hero__title" data-hero-title>
      <span data-hero-title-a>{{ first_word }}</span>
      {%- if rest_words != blank -%}
        <span data-hero-title-b>{{ rest_words }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </h1>

    <div class="hero__frame" data-hero-frame>
      <div class="hero__media" data-hero-media>
        {%- comment -%}
          The poster is a real <img>, always rendered. If the video fails to
          load or autoplay is blocked, this stays visible — never an empty
          black rectangle.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if poster != blank -%}
          <img
            src="{{ poster | image_url: width: 1600 }}"
            srcset="
              {{ poster | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w,
              {{ poster | image_url: width: 1600 }} 1600w
            "
            sizes="(min-width: 1100px) 1550px, 95vw"
            alt="{{ section.settings.video_alt | default: heading | escape }}"
            width="{{ poster.width }}"
            height="{{ poster.height }}"
            class="hero__poster"
            decoding="async"
          >
        {%- else -%}
          {% render 'media-placeholder', label: '' %}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if video != blank -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Sources carry data-src, not src. pawly-hero's script promotes them
            once it has decided the connection and viewport can afford it —
            below 480px, or on Save-Data, the poster is all that loads.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <video
            data-hero-video
            poster="{% if poster != blank %}{{ poster | image_url: width: 1600 }}{% endif %}"
            muted
            loop
            playsinline
            preload="metadata"
            aria-label="{{ section.settings.video_alt | default: heading | escape }}"
            tabindex="-1"
          >
            {%- for source in video.sources -%}
              {%- if source.format == 'mp4' or source.format == 'webm' -%}
                <source data-src="{{ source.url }}" type="{{ source.mime_type }}">
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </video>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero__content" data-hero-content>
      {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
        <p class="hero__subheading">{{ section.settings.subheading }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.cta_label != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The one shimmer button in this viewport. See CLAUDE.md §6 —
          if every button shimmers, none of them do.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {% render 'shimmer-button',
          label: section.settings.cta_label,
          href: section.settings.cta_link,
          icon: 'icon-arrow'
        %}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.footnote != blank -%}
        <p class="hero__footnote">{{ section.settings.footnote }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="hero__scroll-hint" data-hero-hint aria-hidden="true">
      <span>{{ 'sections.hero.scroll_hint' | t }}</span>
      {% render 'icon-chevron-down' %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  (function () {
    var section = document.getElementById('hero-{{ section.id }}');
    if (!section) return;

    var stage = section.querySelector('[data-hero-stage]');
    var bg = section.querySelector('[data-hero-bg]');
    var frame = section.querySelector('[data-hero-frame]');
    var media = section.querySelector('[data-hero-media]');
    var titleA = section.querySelector('[data-hero-title-a]');
    var titleB = section.querySelector('[data-hero-title-b]');
    var content = section.querySelector('[data-hero-content]');
    var hint = section.querySelector('[data-hero-hint]');
    var video = section.querySelector('[data-hero-video]');

    var rtl = (document.dir || document.documentElement.dir) === 'rtl';
    var reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');

    // Read straight from Liquid. This script runs before PawlyConfig is
    // defined at the end of <body>, so it must not depend on it.
    var motionEnabled = {{ settings.motion_enable | json }};
    var DESKTOP_SHIFT = {{ section.settings.desktop_shift | default: 150 }} / 100;
    var MOBILE_SHIFT = {{ section.settings.mobile_shift | default: 180 }} / 100;

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------- video */

    function loadVideo() {
      if (!video) return;

      // Don't spend a visitor's data on decoration.
      var conn = navigator.connection || navigator.mozConnection || navigator.webkitConnection;
      if (conn && conn.saveData) return;
      if (window.innerWidth < 480 && conn && /2g/.test(conn.effectiveType || '')) return;
      if (window.innerWidth < 480 && !conn) return;

      var sources = video.querySelectorAll('source[data-src]');
      if (!sources.length) return;

      sources.forEach(function (s) {
        s.src = s.getAttribute('data-src');
        s.removeAttribute('data-src');
      });

      video.load();

      // If autoplay is refused the poster simply stays. No black rectangle.
      video.addEventListener('canplay', function () {
        video.classList.add('is-ready');
      });

      var play = video.play();
      if (play && play.catch) play.catch(function () {});
    }

    if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) {
      var vio = new IntersectionObserver(
        function (entries) {
          if (entries[0].isIntersecting) {
            loadVideo();
            vio.disconnect();
          }
        },
        { rootMargin: '200px' }
      );
      vio.observe(section);
    } else {
      loadVideo();
    }

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------- motion */

    if (!motionEnabled || reduce.matches) {
      section.classList.add('hero--static');
      return;
    }

    // Closed-state geometry, as a fraction of the open frame.
    var CLOSED_INLINE = 0.4;
    var CLOSED_BLOCK = 0.24;
    var CLOSED_MEDIA_SCALE = 1.28;

    function shiftDistance() {
      // clientWidth, not innerWidth — innerWidth includes the scrollbar
      // gutter, and that is the source of the phantom horizontal overflow.
      var vw = document.documentElement.clientWidth;
      return vw * (vw < 768 ? MOBILE_SHIFT : DESKTOP_SHIFT);
    }

    var state = { p: 0 };

    function apply() {
      var p = state.p;
      var inv = 1 - p;

      if (bg) bg.style.opacity = String(inv);

      if (p > 0.999) {
        // Drop the clip entirely at full open, so the frame's shadow — which a
        // clip-path would otherwise cut away — comes back.
        frame.style.clipPath = 'none';
      } else {
        frame.style.clipPath =
          'inset(' +
          CLOSED_BLOCK * inv * 100 +
          '% ' +
          CLOSED_INLINE * inv * 100 +
          '% round var(--radius-lg))';
      }

      if (media) {
        media.style.transform = 'scale(' + (1 + (CLOSED_MEDIA_SCALE - 1) * inv) + ')';
      }

      // Each half moves outward from centre. In RTL the first word already
      // sits on the right, so it travels right — hence the mirrored sign.
      var d = shiftDistance() * p;
      var sign = rtl ? 1 : -1;
      if (titleA) titleA.style.transform = 'translate3d(' + sign * d + 'px,0,0)';
      if (titleB) titleB.style.transform = 'translate3d(' + -sign * d + 'px,0,0)';

      if (content) {
        var reveal = (p - 0.75) / 0.25;
        reveal = reveal < 0 ? 0 : reveal > 1 ? 1 : reveal;
        content.style.opacity = String(reveal);
        content.style.transform = 'translate3d(0,' + (1 - reveal) * 16 + 'px,0)';
        content.style.pointerEvents = reveal > 0.5 ? 'auto' : 'none';
      }

      // Twice the fade rate of everything else, so the hint is gone by the
      // halfway point and never overlaps the content arriving at 0.75.
      if (hint) hint.style.opacity = String(Math.max(0, 1 - p * 2));
    }

    /** Give up and show the finished hero. Used when GSAP never arrives, and
     *  when the visitor turns reduced-motion on mid-session. */
    function fallbackStatic() {
      [frame, media, titleA, titleB, content, bg, hint].forEach(function (el) {
        if (el) el.removeAttribute('style');
      });
      section.classList.add('hero--static');
    }

    // Collapse synchronously, before the first paint, so the hero is never
    // seen open-then-snapping-shut.
    apply();

    function boot() {
      if (!window.gsap || !window.ScrollTrigger) {
        fallbackStatic();
        return;
      }
      var gsap = window.gsap;
      gsap.registerPlugin(window.ScrollTrigger);

      [frame, media, titleA, titleB].forEach(function (el) {
        if (el) el.style.willChange = 'transform';
      });

      gsap.to(state, {
        p: 1,
        ease: 'none',
        scrollTrigger: {
          trigger: section,
          start: 'top top',
          // Capped at exactly one viewport of scroll, so a touch visitor is
          // never trapped for longer than one swipe and can always scroll up.
          end: '+=100%',
          pin: stage,
          pinSpacing: true,
          scrub: true,
          anticipatePin: 1,
          invalidateOnRefresh: true,
          onUpdate: apply,
          onLeave: function () {
            [frame, media, titleA, titleB].forEach(function (el) {
              if (el) el.style.willChange = 'auto';
            });
          },
          onEnterBack: function () {
            [frame, media, titleA, titleB].forEach(function (el) {
              if (el) el.style.willChange = 'transform';
            });
          }
        }
      });

      // If the visitor turns reduced-motion on mid-session, stand down.
      if (reduce.addEventListener) {
        reduce.addEventListener('change', function () {
          if (!reduce.matches) return;
          window.ScrollTrigger.getAll().forEach(function (st) {
            if (st.trigger === section) st.kill(true);
          });
          fallbackStatic();
        });
      }
    }

    // GSAP is loaded with `defer`, so it may not be parsed yet.
    if (window.gsap && window.ScrollTrigger) {
      boot();
    } else {
      window.addEventListener('load', boot, { once: true });
    }
  })();
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "הירו",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section-hero",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "הכותרת נשברת אחרי המילה הראשונה — שני החצאים נפתחים לצדדים בגלילה. כתבו כותרת שהמילה הראשונה שלה עומדת בפני עצמה."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "כותרת",
      "default": "טיפוח בבית שגם הם אוהבים"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "subheading",
      "label": "תת־כותרת",
      "default": "מברשות, ניקוי כפות ומשחה לכריות. הכול בבית, בלי מספרה ובלי מאבק."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_label",
      "label": "טקסט הכפתור",
      "default": "לכל המוצרים"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "cta_link",
      "label": "קישור הכפתור"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "footnote",
      "label": "שורה מתחת לכפתור",
      "default": "משלוח חינם מעל ₪150 · החזר כספי מלא תוך 90 יום"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "מדיה"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "background",
      "label": "תמונת רקע",
      "info": "בהירה ורכה. רקע כהה מאחורי סרטון בהיר יוצר מלבן חד ומכוער. חתכו ל־21:9."
    },
    {
      "type": "video",
      "id": "video",
      "label": "סרטון",
      "info": "מומלץ עד 2.5MB, 1280×720. נטען רק כשההירו מתקרב למסך, ולא נטען בכלל במסכים קטנים או במצב חיסכון בנתונים."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "poster",
      "label": "תמונת פוסטר",
      "info": "הפריים הראשון של הסרטון. מוצגת אם הסרטון לא נטען או שהדפדפן חוסם ניגון אוטומטי."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "video_alt",
      "label": "תיאור המדיה לקוראי מסך",
      "default": "סרטון קצר של טיפוח בבית"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "תנועה"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "desktop_shift",
      "label": "מרחק פתיחת הכותרת במחשב",
      "min": 100,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 150
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "mobile_shift",
      "label": "מרחק פתיחת הכותרת במובייל",
      "min": 120,
      "max": 220,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 180
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "הירו"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
